{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgANnwWWaVRLzNXBbVLxL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made the fix and the tests pass, but I couldn't commit it: this repo has no git author name or email set. The changes are staged and ready.\n\n**Problem:** `Hijack()` in `response_writer.go` refused to hijack as soon as `Written()` was true. That includes the case where only headers have gone out, via `WriteHeaderNow()` or `Flush()`, with no body yet. WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket`, and middleware that flushes headers before an upgrade, hit `errHijackAlreadyWritten` even though nothing had actually been sent in the body.\n\n**Fix** (`response_writer.go:111`): it now only refuses once body bytes have been written:\n- nothing written yet → hijack allowed (same as before)\n- only headers written → hijack allowed (this used to fail)\n- body bytes written → still returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten`\n\nI added a comment above the method explaining this.\n\n**Tests** (`response_writer_test.go`): I added two cases to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`, one hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` and one after `Flush()`. Both expect the hijack to succeed. The existing \"hijack after write should fail\" case still passes, and `go test ./...` and `gofmt` are clean.\n\nTo commit, set your identity, for example with `git config user.name \"…\"` and `git config user.email \"…\"`, and run `git commit` with your title. I can then commit it with a fuller message if you'd like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":34990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c112f836-5a84-4096-9996-f0f00167faa1","uuid":"81a62077-3847-47b1-b9c3-a3de72f0047a","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:01:07.973Z","request_id":"req_011CgANnwKbagCK8taTRKkk9"}
{"duration_api_ms":29164,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c112f836-5a84-4096-9996-f0f00167faa1","total_cost_usd":0.2532702,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35444,"cache_read_input_tokens":130451,"output_tokens":2496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":812},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":35444},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":34990,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2496,"cacheReadInputTokens":130451,"cacheCreationInputTokens":35444,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2532702,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":812,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I made the fix and the tests pass, but I couldn't commit it: this repo has no git author name or email set. The changes are staged and ready.\n\n**Problem:** `Hijack()` in `response_writer.go` refused to hijack as soon as `Written()` was true. That includes the case where only headers have gone out, via `WriteHeaderNow()` or `Flush()`, with no body yet. WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket`, and middleware that flushes headers before an upgrade, hit `errHijackAlreadyWritten` even though nothing had actually been sent in the body.\n\n**Fix** (`response_writer.go:111`): it now only refuses once body bytes have been written:\n- nothing written yet → hijack allowed (same as before)\n- only headers written → hijack allowed (this used to fail)\n- body bytes written → still returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten`\n\nI added a comment above the method explaining this.\n\n**Tests** (`response_writer_test.go`): I added two cases to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`, one hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` and one after `Flush()`. Both expect the hijack to succeed. The existing \"hijack after write should fail\" case still passes, and `go test ./...` and `gofmt` are clean.\n\nTo commit, set your identity, for example with `git config user.name \"…\"` and `git config user.email \"…\"`, and run `git commit` with your title. I can then commit it with a fuller message if you'd like.","ttft_ms":5210,"type":"result","duration_ms":35001,"uuid":"6e852e98-2f3b-40f9-b1be-2c873ada87ec","ttft_stream_ms":2326,"time_to_request_ms":213,"first_content_frame_ms":2326,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
